WEBVTT

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.310
Hey, come on, wait up!

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:07.940
What could be all the way
down here in the legs?

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:10.150
Haven't you noticed?

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:13.400
This body hasn't gotten
any sleep for two full days.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:19.330
WHITE BLOOD CELL

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:14.530
What?

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:16.660
It's been in the same position, too, no less.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.330
But that sounds pretty serious, right?

00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:24.540
Just as I thought.

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:12.190
EPISODE 8:
CALVES, PULMONARY EMBOLISM,
AND QUICK THINKING

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:12.190
I've come to deliver your oxygen!

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:13.940
Right!

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:16.940
Oh, so it's you?

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:19.660
If you could stamp this receipt, please...

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:22.660
Hey, by the way, I heard!

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:23.700
Heard what?

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:29.370
CELL

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:26.250
Is it true that you got
some kind of award?

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:27.500
Uh, yeah.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.370
What kind of award?
What kind of award?

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:33.880
It's called the "Top Rookie Award."

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:35.840
Oh yeah?

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:37.840
Look, don't get all full of yourself!

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:38.550
Huh?

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:42.390
I can't tell you how many Red Blood Cells
I've seen showered with praise in their youth,

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:45.760
only to stop trying, and end up useless!

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:49.390
Well, but I don't think
I'm acting all full of myself.

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:51.190
- I refuse to acknowledge you.
- Huh?

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:54.440
It's going to be a long time
before I acknowledge you, all right?

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:56.940
What are you waiting for?
Go deliver that oxygen already!

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.070
R-Right!

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:04.410
Just keep on giving it your all, okay?

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:08.950
Yo! Long time no see!

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:10.870
Hey, you're looking pretty good!

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:14.290
I've got the caffeine out of my system,
so I'm back in business!

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:16.380
For real? That's good to hear!

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:20.970
Carbon monoxide! Run!

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:27.890
For heaven's sake, what's going on here?

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:33.190
I get myself back on the job,
but now there's even more smoking than ever.

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:35.560
How can we be expected
to deliver oxygen like this?

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:37.780
You said it.

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:39.030
Hey, you two!

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:40.490
So, you survived?

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:43.700
- Oh, uh, thanks for your hard work!
- Thanks for your hard work!

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:48.080
Since I saw you last,
you seem to have manned up a lot.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:49.250
Huh? You really think—

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:50.370
Hey, thanks!

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:52.750
Nah, I wasn't talking to you.

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:54.210
Seriously?

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:56.090
I'm just kidding!

00:03:56.090 --> 00:04:01.090
The Red Blood Cell numbers are down,
so we're looking to you young guys to step up!

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:03.590
Especially in times like these.

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:12.690
Alcohol now?

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:17.190
I guess there's no way around it. Why don't we
have some lovely ladies detox us in the liver?

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:20.690
Hey, I haven't been there in ages!
I vote yes!

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:24.660
LIVER

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:24.660
Huh?

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:28.620
ACTIVATE
VITAMINS & MINERALS!

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.620
This is that liver?

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:31.580
But it was so lively last time.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:34.040
It looks like a lot of places are shuttered.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:36.500
BLOOD ALLEY
BILE TOWN
FIRST AVENUE

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:36.500
It sure seems desolate now.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:40.460
On top of that, it's all sticky with oil!

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:43.340
Is Hepatocyte okay?

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:49.180
Three guests have arrived.

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:53.980
No way!

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:58.110
Hey, what happened
to all the glitz and glamor?

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:07.110
Welcome, Red Blood Cells.

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:11.200
H-Hepatocyte!

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:15.040
Hey, are you all right?

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:17.790
I'm so sorry you have to see
the place in such disarray.

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:21.750
There's been a surge in triglycerides
thanks to all that alcohol,

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:24.510
so the liver's functions
have been impaired.

00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:27.510
<i>Fatty liver.</i>

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:33.100
<i>When there's excess fat buildup
of more than 30% in the liver.</i>

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:37.690
<i>Often caused by alcoholism,
it prevents the liver from functioning normally,</i>

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:42.690
<i>and if left unchecked, it can lead
to hepatic cirrhosis or liver cancer.</i>

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:46.860
Are you all right, Hepatocyte?

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:52.830
I guess I can't really help you Red Blood Cells
heal if I'm in this state.

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:56.290
Hey! Somebody give us a hand here!

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:59.170
We don't have enough people
to deliver oxygen!

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:01.590
Right, gotcha! We're coming!

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:05.340
What? Not even a short break for us?

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:07.260
We'll come back another time.

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:09.050
I'm really sorry.

00:06:10.590 --> 00:06:12.140
Please take care of yourself.

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:19.480
Ugh... So exhausting...

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:24.480
We're almost there. It's up to young guys
like you and me to step up now!

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:30.820
I can't step up anymore!

00:06:32.700 --> 00:06:34.790
We finally reached the calf, huh?

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:37.580
Let's take a break now, all right?

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:41.170
I mean, there's an even steeper climb up ahead!

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:43.630
Yeah, but I think it'll be easier.

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:46.260
Since the pressure from the calves
will be pushing our backs.

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:48.260
Huh? I didn't know that.

00:06:48.260 --> 00:07:01.980
MUSCLE

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:50.720
<i>The calves.</i>

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:59.270
<i>Because the calf muscles pump the blood
pooled in the lower torso back to the heart,</i>

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:01.980
<i>they're also known
as the body's second heart.</i>

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:07.690
Well, what do we have here?
Hey, it's the rookies!

00:07:07.690 --> 00:07:12.530
Look at you, diligently transporting oxygen
again today... Such heroes!

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:14.620
We should take a page from your book!

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:16.240
Come on.

00:07:16.950 --> 00:07:20.250
But we were such good buddies!
How cold is that?

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:23.830
I bet you're jonesing for some caffeine
about now, am I right?

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:26.750
Let's go get drenched again sometime!

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:29.920
You were a lot more energetic back then!

00:07:31.930 --> 00:07:33.390
- Excuse me.
- Huh?

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:38.350
I don't really care one way or another
how you two choose to work.

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:43.650
But if you could just stop dragging down cells
who take their jobs seriously, that'd be great!

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:44.480
Hey...

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:53.110
No wonder you're the winner
of the Top Rookie Award.

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:55.160
What a stirring speech!

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:57.910
Oh yeah, couldn't agree more!

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:03.870
We only said that for his own good, you know.
We weren't trying to drag him down.

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:07.380
Would you mind not having
anything to do with him anymore?

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:10.130
Sure, roger that!

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:10.920
Let's go.

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:12.840
O-Okay.

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:16.050
I can't stand them.

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:21.310
Straight-arrow squirts like that
bursting with self-righteousness...

00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:24.940
This hill is murder!

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:27.900
I think it's even more exhausting
than the one before!

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:30.110
I don't get it.

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:35.610
Normally, we'd get pushed forward by the blood
pressure from the calves, so it's an easier climb.

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:39.330
Not only that, but thanks to dehydration,
the ground's all grungy!

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:41.250
This is so gross!

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:48.790
The blood vessel's so fragile now
that it's crumbling?

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:50.550
Are you okay?

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:52.800
Is this...

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:54.260
a blood clot?

00:08:55.800 --> 00:08:57.260
<i>Blood clot.</i>

00:08:57.260 --> 00:09:00.850
<i>When blood coagulates
within a blood vessel.</i>

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:05.310
<i>Formed when the vessel wall
is damaged or becomes inflamed.</i>

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:10.230
<i>Because it hinders blood circulation,
it can lead to various ailments.</i>

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:14.610
That blood clot formed
because of the pool of fallen Red Blood Cells!

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:18.240
<i>Deep-vein thrombosis.</i>

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:21.660
<i>When a blood clot forms
in the veins of the lower torso.</i>

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:24.370
<i>Caused when the legs are immobile
for extended periods of time,</i>

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:28.080
<i>or by damage or inflammation
to the vessel walls.</i>

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:30.790
If we were to fall into a place like this...

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:34.170
Look out!

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:40.430
So close.

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:42.140
You guys...

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:44.350
What the heck do you think you're doing?

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:49.810
I happened to drop my oxygen.
I was hoping you could go get it for me.

00:09:52.150 --> 00:09:55.190
Since you two take your jobs so seriously,

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:57.950
that wouldn't be a problem
at all, would it?

00:09:57.950 --> 00:09:59.200
This is insane!

00:09:59.530 --> 00:10:02.620
Now's the time for us to give it our all,
and you're pulling a stunt like this?

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:04.750
Don't make us laugh.

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:09.500
For a body whose health is deteriorating
by the minute no matter how hard we work,

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:11.880
how are we supposed to give it our all?

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:14.090
Tell us, why don't you?

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:18.340
Whether or not you work your silly little
butts off, it doesn't change a thing!

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:22.760
But don't you dare ever mouth off at us again!

00:10:27.690 --> 00:10:29.650
Dammit!

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:38.400
White Blood Cell?

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:40.160
Are you all right?

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:43.740
You saved us.

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:47.790
Thank you so much, White Blood Cell.

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:49.750
No need to thank me.

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:54.710
But seriously, you're always rescuing us.

00:10:54.710 --> 00:10:56.460
It's a two-way street.

00:10:57.460 --> 00:10:59.050
Is it really?

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:02.300
For now, let's just get you away from here.

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:09.560
But really...

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:12.480
I can't believe
there's such a gaping hole there.

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:15.770
Don't let your guard down as you move on.

00:11:15.770 --> 00:11:19.240
Because that spot back there
isn't the only place where there's a blood clot.

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:20.740
Huh? Really?

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:23.530
I found a bunch of other clots
on my way here.

00:11:24.030 --> 00:11:25.700
How did things get so bad?

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:31.120
Through excessive consumption
of nutrients five, six times a day.

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:35.590
Also, this body hasn't had any sleep
for two full days now,

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:38.130
and it's been in the same position
all that time, barely moving.

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:40.130
Huh? Two full days?

00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:43.510
So, that's why the calf muscles
have hardly been functioning,

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:46.810
and the blood pressure that should be
pushing upward was so weak.

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:50.020
What's all this shaking?

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:55.060
The calf muscles are finally starting to move!

00:11:56.070 --> 00:11:58.030
Hey, great!

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:01.900
Meaning that the blood pressure will rise,
so it'll be easier for us to climb, right?

00:12:13.870 --> 00:12:14.540
Huh?

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:18.000
Whoa! What the cell is that?

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:23.220
Run into the capillary!

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:28.640
What the...

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:31.100
...h-heck was that?

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:36.360
That was the blood clot rolling out,
fanned by the sudden rise in blood pressure.

00:12:37.270 --> 00:12:41.320
If that blood clot were to get stuck
in some crucial organ somewhere...

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:43.320
there could be trouble.

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:45.450
We have to stop it!

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:48.910
Hey! Hold up!

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:50.370
We have a problem!

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:51.700
What's going on?

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:55.620
The blood clot that formed in the deep vein
is not hurtling toward the upper torso!

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:56.630
What did you say?

00:12:57.080 --> 00:12:58.840
Just where is it heading?

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:01.050
The pulmonary artery!

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:12.770
Did you see those rookies' faces?

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:14.810
So panicked, it was hysterical!

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:17.400
I bet they learned their lesson.

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:20.770
That's what happens to rookies
who have the nerve to mouth off.

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:24.320
Huh? What's going on?

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:30.450
Something huge is coming this way!

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:30.450
PLATELETS

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:32.450
No way! What is it?

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:34.960
Oh! So scary!

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:36.420
Don't run away, morons!

00:13:37.170 --> 00:13:39.040
We've got to hold it off and—

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:41.590
Not happening, not happening!

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:49.930
Come on, not that thing!

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:54.140
So, that blood clot
hasn't come to a stop yet?

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:57.810
It's no good! The blood clot
is still heading toward the lungs!

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:04.320
Hey, it's not safe! Up ahead is...

00:14:04.610 --> 00:14:06.740
PULMONARY
ARTERY

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:06.740
The pulmonary artery!

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:11.030
<i>Stop!</i>

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:15.700
Stop!

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:20.040
What was that just now?

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:20.960
WELCOME TO THE LUNGS

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:23.000
What on earth is going on?

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:32.640
We were too late.

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:35.430
LUNGS

00:14:35.930 --> 00:14:37.310
The blood clot...

00:14:37.730 --> 00:14:39.600
is stuck now!

00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:45.110
What are you doing?
We have to get that clot out of there!

00:14:45.110 --> 00:14:47.070
R-Right!

00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:55.790
It's no good! It's not even budging!

00:14:57.540 --> 00:14:58.910
Are you all right?

00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:07.630
So, you got caught up
in the blood clot as it rolled by?

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:12.850
How lame is this?

00:15:12.850 --> 00:15:16.390
Th-The pulmonary artery's clogged up.

00:15:16.390 --> 00:15:20.270
Now we can't deliver oxygen to the lungs!

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:23.730
The light...

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:26.650
<i>Economy Class Syndrome.</i>

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:29.860
<i>Also known as "pulmonary embolism."</i>

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:35.280
<i>When a blood clot in the lower torso</i>

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:38.660
PULMONARY
ARTERY

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:38.660
<i>makes its way to the lungs via the bloodstream.</i>

00:15:39.330 --> 00:15:41.960
<i>As a result, the blood stops flowing
to the pulmonary alveolus,</i>

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:47.460
<i>preventing the Red Blood Cells
from transporting oxygen, thus triggering hypoxia.</i>

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:51.130
<i>Causes shortness of breath and chest pain.</i>

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:53.890
<i>In some cases, it can lead to death.</i>

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:57.890
Can you believe this?

00:15:58.310 --> 00:16:00.480
The pulmonary artery's blocked!

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:04.860
At this rate, the lungs will be destroyed, and
we won't be able to get any oxygen from the lungs!

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:07.110
Oxygen levels across the whole body
are plunging!

00:16:08.480 --> 00:16:11.320
If this keeps up, this body will...

00:16:11.900 --> 00:16:13.320
It's all over now!

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:16.160
We're both going to die!

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:24.790
This crappy world is history now!

00:16:32.930 --> 00:16:34.840
What should we do?

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:39.310
How can we overcome this crisis?

00:16:39.770 --> 00:16:44.140
White Blood Cell, you have to save us!
How can we deal with this?

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:51.190
We White Blood Cells are effective in battle
against external enemies.

00:16:51.820 --> 00:16:55.490
The only ones who can get us
out of this predicament are actually...

00:16:55.870 --> 00:16:58.030
What can we do?

00:16:59.290 --> 00:17:01.080
The bronchial arteries.

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:03.540
Bronchial arteries?

00:17:05.120 --> 00:17:08.420
We'll go through the bronchial arteries
to deliver oxygen to the lungs!

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:12.420
But those aren't blood vessels
for gas exchange, are they?

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:15.130
No way can we transport such
a massive load of oxygen!

00:17:15.970 --> 00:17:17.800
<i>The bronchial arteries.</i>

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:21.600
<i>Unlike the pulmonary arteries,
which specialize in gas exchange,</i>

00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:23.730
<i>and through which
massive amounts of blood flow,</i>

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:28.150
<i>these are narrow vessels which deliver oxygen
and nutrients to the pulmonary alveolus itself</i>

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:31.980
<i>and other respiratory organs
via a separate route.</i>

00:17:32.820 --> 00:17:36.860
All we have to do is hold on until this blood clot
dissolves and the circulation is restored!

00:17:36.860 --> 00:17:39.990
We have to supply
as much oxygen as we can!

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:42.200
I'm telling you, that's crazy!

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:44.660
Everyone, can you help us out?

00:17:45.410 --> 00:17:47.370
Let's deliver oxygen to the lungs!

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:57.510
Well, of course I'll go.

00:17:57.510 --> 00:17:59.260
I'll go, all right.

00:18:03.100 --> 00:18:07.560
This is a job that no one
but you guys can carry out.

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:09.940
We're leaving this body to you.

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:11.570
Right!

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:15.650
BRONCHIAL ARTERY
6 - 12

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:17.490
So cramped.

00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:20.620
I don't think we can deliver
oxygen through here.

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:25.830
<i>The bronchial arteries are no more
than one to two millimeters thick.</i>

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:31.090
<i>The amount of blood flowing through them is only 1%
or so of what flows through the pulmonary arteries.</i>

00:18:31.840 --> 00:18:34.170
However, we have no choice but to do it.

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:35.970
Let's all work together!

00:18:38.010 --> 00:18:39.010
Let's go!

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:53.150
I'm not kidding, man. A place like this...

00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:58.110
<i>Please let us get there in time!</i>

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:05.080
It's been a while since they left,
but there's no response.

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:07.450
I guess it was a crazy idea, after all!

00:19:13.130 --> 00:19:15.170
The blood clot's starting to dissolve!

00:19:16.260 --> 00:19:17.670
Hey, now we can move on!

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:19.380
Everybody, deliver that oxygen!

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:22.180
<i>What happened to the Lung Cells...</i>

00:19:22.930 --> 00:19:24.470
<i>and the rookies?</i>

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:31.310
Too late...

00:19:35.900 --> 00:19:38.030
We're fine.

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:43.660
We're all just lying here
to preserve our strength.

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:46.410
But how?

00:19:47.160 --> 00:19:53.960
It was just a trickle, but we started to get
a supply of oxygen from the bronchial arteries,

00:19:53.960 --> 00:19:56.840
and that's how we were able to survive.

00:19:56.840 --> 00:19:58.130
Thank goodness!

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:01.090
So, the blood clot dissolved, right?

00:20:02.090 --> 00:20:03.890
It was all thanks to them.

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:08.140
Everyone! Please bring some oxygen
to those people over there, too!

00:20:22.910 --> 00:20:27.240
Man, I'm wiped!
I can't move anymore!

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:30.910
But look. Thanks to the ample
supply of oxygen...

00:20:33.120 --> 00:20:35.920
This is the good kind of exhaustion, huh?

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:38.880
True that.

00:20:41.050 --> 00:20:44.220
Didn't I tell you it was a two-way street?

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:48.310
You guys just pulled off something
that we couldn't do.

00:20:48.930 --> 00:20:51.680
You saved the day. I appreciate it.

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:52.940
Thanks.

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:54.810
Right!

00:20:58.730 --> 00:21:00.070
<i>That's right.</i>

00:21:00.070 --> 00:21:03.990
<i>Because of the situation we're in,
as coworkers in the same body...</i>

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:08.410
<i>we have to join forces
and help each other out.</i>

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:11.370
<i>Precisely because of the situation we're in.</i>

00:21:26.010 --> 00:21:26.930
Something's...

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:28.720
not right!

00:21:36.060 --> 00:21:37.520
I don't believe this!

00:21:38.520 --> 00:21:40.230
The White Blood Cells are...

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:42.400
nowhere to be seen!

00:21:44.490 --> 00:21:46.070
Just what in the world...

00:21:48.370 --> 00:21:51.410
is happening to this body?

00:23:19.500 --> 00:23:21.500
PREVIEW

00:23:20.040 --> 00:23:23.380
I want you to be even more vigilant than ever
about bacteria and viruses!

00:23:22.420 --> 00:23:23.380
CALAMITY

00:23:23.380 --> 00:23:25.840
What the heck is this?

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:26.130
ATHLETE'S FOOT

00:23:25.840 --> 00:23:28.800
Those sturdy walls on the bottoms
of the feet are full of holes!

00:23:28.800 --> 00:23:29.970
THE MEANING OF WORK

00:23:28.800 --> 00:23:31.090
We're all exhausted!

00:23:31.090 --> 00:23:33.390
As if we have any time to rest!

00:23:31.090 --> 00:23:34.010
CALAMITY, ATHLETE'S FOOT,
AND THE MEANING OF WORK
